// The simulated system: the target a scenario runs, and the channel policies
// that decide what the runner feeds and what it logs.
//
// No `generate` attribute, and that is forced rather than stylistic: the
// grammar admits a `system_target` only in a module that generates nothing. So
// the process, the machine it runs on and the box they host are declared in
// `sim.clk`, and this file names the target over them and emits only the
// process description and per-domain configs the runner reads.
//
// What a scenario needs from this file is the two per-domain configs: the
// channel publisher config that makes the schedule and injection channels come
// out of an input log, and the event logger config that puts every channel
// worth asserting on into the output log.
//
// The policies live here rather than beside the channels they bind because
// `channel_policy` generates nothing, and a module that generates C++ may not
// import one that generates no targets.
//
// Everything a scenario checker reads is below. `DriverPose` is the machine's
// heartbeat, `DriverCmd` what it was asked for, `DriverEvt` what the gate did
// about it, `TickFaults` what the decision tick had to say and `Estimates`
// where the head was. The two log-fed channels are logged as well, so a run's
// inputs and its outputs are in one file and a failure can be read without the
// scenario's source in hand.

use cogs::sim;
use cogs::motion;
use @clockwork::clockwork::logging::channel_policy::{ChannelLoggingPolicy,
    LogReaderPolicy, LogType};

// What makes the runner publish these two channels from the input log. Neither
// policy carries a `source_name`, so the source is the channel's own name,
// which is what the scenario author writes.
policy LogReaderPolicy for motion::ScheduleChan
{
}

policy LogReaderPolicy for sim::SimCmdChan
{
}

// What the run is asked to do, kept beside what it did.
policy ChannelLoggingPolicy for motion::ScheduleChan
{
    log_type = LogType::event;
}

policy ChannelLoggingPolicy for sim::SimCmdChan
{
    log_type = LogType::event;
}

// The machine's heartbeat: one sample per cycle, always.
policy ChannelLoggingPolicy for motion::DriverPose
{
    log_type = LogType::event;
}

// What it was asked to hold next.
policy ChannelLoggingPolicy for motion::DriverCmd
{
    log_type = LogType::event;
}

// What the gate did that the sample stream does not show.
policy ChannelLoggingPolicy for sim::DriverEvt
{
    log_type = LogType::event;
}

// What the decision tick raised.
policy ChannelLoggingPolicy for motion::TickFaults
{
    log_type = LogType::event;
}

// Where the head was, once per sample.
policy ChannelLoggingPolicy for motion::Estimates
{
    log_type = LogType::event;
}

system_target motion_sim
{
    box: sim::System;
}
